## Vercel Speed Insights Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the FactLens frontend application.

### Changes Made

1. **Package Installation**
   - Installed `@vercel/speed-insights` v2.0.0 package via npm
   - Updated `package.json` to include the new dependency
   - Updated `package-lock.json` with dependency resolution

2. **HTML Integration** (`index.html`)
   - Added Speed Insights initialization script in the `<head>` section
   - Placed it immediately after the existing Vercel Web Analytics script
   - Follows the vanilla HTML/JavaScript implementation pattern from official docs
   - Script tags:
     - Initialization: `window.si` function setup
     - Script loader: `/_vercel/speed-insights/script.js` (deferred loading)

3. **Analytics Helper Update** (`analytics.js`)
   - Updated comments to reflect both Web Analytics and Speed Insights
   - Added Speed Insights initialization fallback for local development
   - Maintains consistency with existing Web Analytics pattern

### Implementation Details

This is a vanilla JavaScript/HTML project, so I followed the official Vercel Speed Insights documentation for non-framework applications. The implementation uses the standard Vercel CDN path pattern (`/_vercel/speed-insights/script.js`) which automatically serves the Speed Insights tracking script when deployed on Vercel.

The initialization script creates a queue (`window.siq`) similar to the Web Analytics implementation, ensuring that any Speed Insights calls made before the script loads are queued and executed once the script is ready.

### Files Modified
- `frontend/package.json` - Added @vercel/speed-insights dependency
- `frontend/package-lock.json` - Updated with new package resolution
- `frontend/index.html` - Added Speed Insights script tags
- `frontend/analytics.js` - Added Speed Insights initialization

### Verification
- ✓ JavaScript syntax validated for all modified JS files
- ✓ HTML structure verified
- ✓ Package installed successfully
- ✓ No build errors
- ✓ Lock file updated correctly

### Next Steps
Once deployed to Vercel, Speed Insights will automatically begin tracking Core Web Vitals and performance metrics. No additional configuration is required. Performance data will appear in the Vercel dashboard under the Speed Insights section within a few days of user traffic.
